    "body": "fix on issue/994-cycle-hop-level · PR #1019 (stacked on #1002) · pinned by cycle_hop::{every_cycle_post_traverses_between_holes_at_the_hop, a_cycle_anchored_on_the_rapid_to_r_is_seated_first, the_checker_catches_the_r_plane_traverse} + script_{fanuc,haas,mazak,sinumerik,tormach,doosan_dnm}::drill_retract + app nc/drill_plate.nc · merges when reviewed\n\nFindings: the six cycle posts swallowed every rapid after a cycle until section end and read G98 with the tool already on R. Fix: the chain is only what stays on the hole (XY, at or below R); the first leaving rapid ends the group (G80) and posts as the stream says; G99 per group (Sinumerik: tool seated on R, no return word); a cut leaving the hole in a group is refused by name. The lathe face-drilling exit has the same shape and is filed as #1011.",
